  "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14264109/assets/8bc549c68a3bc5b7989ac1835e4bb58183066c7797264b8cccd4f3fd2c895056.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The domain of the function is all the real numbers except for the points $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since the period of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ is $\\pi $, we have $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+n\\pi )=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ for any integer $n.$ Thus, for $n=-1,$ we get $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\pi ).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The lines $x=n\\pi $ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Thus, $x=-5\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote.",
